<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackageId>Harbor.Tui.CellForge.Engine</PackageId>
    <Description>Harbor TUI engine — terminal input layer (kitty keyboard, SGR mouse, bracketed paste), byte state-machine parser, cell rendering primitives. BCL-only, AOT-compatible. Namespaces stay Harbor.Tui.CellForge.* (issue #33 split). Standalone leaf since #436: zero ProjectReference entries to Harbor assemblies and zero per-file imports of Harbor namespaces — the cell/input/probe vocabulary the engine uses lives here as engine-owned ports (verbatim copies), and the chat-owned rendering (prompt/composer/markdown/overlay/layout/image-layer) moved to Harbor.Tui.CellForge/Chat/Rendering. History: #795 deleted the project-wide global using that hid the borrows; #435 removed Harbor.Abstractions (dead by fact) and Harbor.Ui.Framework.State (ported onto the BCL-only UiKeyDto (#162) and EnterDecision vocabularies); #436 ported the remaining 15 cell/input/probe types and moved the chat files out. See CellForgeEngineAtomicityRules, which now guards the achieved state.</Description>
    <PackageTags>harbor;tui;terminal;input;kitty-keyboard;sgr-mouse;bracketed-paste</PackageTags>
    <!-- CellForge must stay trim/AOT-clean: analyzers enforce zero IL2xxx warnings at build time. -->
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- #436 RED: both edges dropped, nothing else fixed on purpose. This commit
         exists to be red — the compiler's own error list is the instrument.
         Harbor.Ui.Framework.Rendering carried the cell/screen/input/Markdown/
         widget vocabulary (Cell, Rect, ScreenBuffer, CellStyle, KeyEvent family,
         MdLine/MdStyle, ChatPalette, PanelFx, CellDiffHints, UiStageCounters);
         Harbor.DesignSystem carried the OSC-11 probe (TerminalBackgroundProbe)
         EscapeSequenceParser binds. Per the #1009 measurement the DesignSystem
         edge is redundant-by-transit (its five bound types resolve through the
         Rendering edge) — deleting BOTH at once verifies that, and verifies no
         third carrier (Contracts via Rendering→Contracts, State is already gone
         per #435) hides behind them. Ports land in the next commits. -->
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Harbor.Tui.CellForge"/>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Harbor.Tui.CellForge.Tests"/>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
